 "notes": [
  "Tolerance is half a unit in the last quoted decimal place, so a claim quoted to one decimal is allowed 0.05.",
  "'Harmonized clinical external gain' is stated as an upper bound ('<= 0.3 points') and is checked as one: the gain is -0.14 under the five-class restriction and +0.29 unrestricted.",
  "The pCR delta is the paired-bootstrap mean of the per-sample AUC difference, not the difference of the two point AUCs (which is 0.0028); the paired estimate is the appropriate one.",
  "The manuscript's harmonized-clinical TCGA delta is -0.14, recomputed from full precision (80.4035 - 80.5476 = -0.1441). An earlier draft stated -0.15, which came from taking the difference of the two values after rounding them to two decimals (80.40 - 80.55); corrected in manuscript.tex.",
  "Scope: the audit covers quantitative claims in the abstract, Results, tables and the submission checklist. It does not cover per-fold values inside the result files, nor quantities the manuscript reports only qualitatively."
 ],
